 for him to take anyone  else seriously with humans lucifer is  like a cat playing with a mouse he  barely puts forward any effort outside  of batting away punches and using his  enemies moves against them it's always  clear that he could crush them at any  time but chooses not to true to form  lucifer would much rather talk  manipulate or seduce his way out of a  gem rather than get in a physical fight  but even when celestial beings and other  supernaturally powered creatures get  involved lucifer is still dominant on  top of beating menadil and michael two  of the most powerful angels in existence  lucifer also easily overpowers maize one  of hell's most skilled and ruthless  demons portrayed by leslie anne brandt  the fight only ended because lucifer had  decided he was finished  it's honestly impossible to say how old  lucifer is he existed even before the  creation of the universe and his  lifespan is infinite this is one of the  many reasons he tried to fill his  endless life with every perceivable  pleasure before he met chloe and made  some real friends of course he is immune  to everything that kills humans aging  negative physical conditions genetic and  contractible illnesses and poisons and  toxins they simply don't affect him  lucifer's immunity to poisons and toxins  has an interesting side effect it's  almost impossible for him to get drunk  or be affected by mind-altering  substances  though it's not for lack of trying as  the owner of lux lucifer regularly  drinks and is known for mixing a mean  cocktail but he drinks more for the  camaraderie and the taste than the  effects while he can be affected by  mind-altering substances his angel  physiology burns it out of him so  quickly he requires superhuman amounts  to just catch a buzz what humans might  see as a gift however  lucifer often mourns are you drunk i  wish  pesky supernatural metabolism keeps  getting in the way don't don't stop me  trying now  along with his immunity he is virtually  indestructible he is able to physically  withstand any amount of damage a human  or other creature could inflict multiple  times throughout the series lucifer  received bullet and stab wounds that  would easily kill anyone else he  casually tells a group of gunmen in the  pilot episode  yes well don't waste your munitions i'm  immortal  it should be noted that for a few  seasons chloe was basically lucifer's  kryptonite and physical proximity to her  would render him vulnerable to attack  and more prone to being impaired however  after this was resolved the only known  objects that could actually kill him  were the flaming sword a divine weapon  powerful enough to kill any being in the  universe and demon daggers which are  forged in hell  during his time on earth lucifer prefers  to use his beautiful human face for  obvious reasons not only is he deeply  vain but he's trying to pass for humans  so he has to look the part while in this  form it can be easy to forget he's a  fallen angel and the king of hell but  lucifer has the ability to shapeshift  into multiple versions of his terrifying  demon form this can range from simply  turning his eyes into fiery orbs  revealing his scarred demonic face or  becoming his final form as the king of  hell complete with leathery clawed wings  when lucifer doesn't physically change  shape he can still manage to push a  mental image of his demon form into any  human's mind to terrify them while  lucifer is mostly in control of his  physical appearance it is also linked  directly to his psychological state his  scarred and twisted visage is an outer  reflection of his inner turmoil and  reveals how he feels about himself  despite his devil may care attitude  lucifer actually suffers from an  enormous amount of guilt over the things  he's done and the torture he's forced to  inflict as hell's ruler this is also  reflected in his complicated love-hate  relationship with his wings  lucifer retained his angelic feathered  wings when he 